      "title": "4.3. Choosing a Redundancy Measure",
      "gist": "No single agreed-upon measure of redundant information exists; nearly a dozen competing functions trade off scope and assumptions, and most neuroscience studies reviewed here rely on the original, sometimes criticized, Imin measure.",
