      "title": "6. Practical Considerations in PID",
      "gist": "Applying PID requires matching a redundancy measure to data type, ensuring enough data to estimate probabilities reliably, choosing among available software tools, and recognizing the framework's interpretive and scaling limits.",
      "question": "PID analysis — what practical choices and limitations must researchers weigh before applying partial information decomposition to real data? (a practical guide)",
      "sourceHeading": "6. Practical Considerations in PID"
    },
