      "title": "6.3. Practical Limitations of the PID Framework",
      "gist": "The number of distinct information atoms explodes combinatorially with more parent neurons, making complete decomposition intractable, and like all information measures, PID also suffers from finite-sample bias in estimating entropy and mutual information.",
      "sourceHeading": "6.3. Practical Limitations of the PID Framework"
